                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0e6e45d3-2819-3372-be6f-89ddc8e5a333",
                        "entry_id": "a0a1a4ec-dbab-3740-a486-fe5bc80d124c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "in einem gewissen Sinn"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "354b9cc3-3076-4b6d-be46-639f71946b0d",
                                "sense_id": "0e6e45d3-2819-3372-be6f-89ddc8e5a333",
                                "text": "Ich bin gewissermaßen mit Öl an den Fingern aufgewachsen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "442889f7-808f-42ff-b5e3-f51a318693ea",
                                "sense_id": "0e6e45d3-2819-3372-be6f-89ddc8e5a333",
                                "text": "Die Preisgabe des Bankgeheimnisses ist für das Land ein schmerzhafter Prozess, nicht nur wegen seiner wirtschaftlichen Bedeutung, sondern auch weil es für viele Schweizer gewissermaßen zur nationalen Identität gehört."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "62d5579f-d5af-4a0e-947c-c52c262ff192",
                        "source_entry_id": "a0a1a4ec-dbab-3740-a486-fe5bc80d124c",
                        "source_sense_id": "0e6e45d3-2819-3372-be6f-89ddc8e5a333",
                        "source_sense_description": "in einem gewissen Sinn",
                        "target_lang_word": "as it were",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "as it were",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2710d9e-7caf-35bd-8b14-041b9420adea",
                                        "entry_id": "4612d932-69cf-355d-b329-9224f97fbad0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see as, it, were."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2077c22-c50d-33af-a309-48cc138b2810",
                                        "entry_id": "4612d932-69cf-355d-b329-9224f97fbad0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to indicate that a word or statement is perhaps not exact though practically right; as if it were so."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64283404-b45c-411b-920a-7a18c34b4706",
                                                "sense_id": "c2077c22-c50d-33af-a309-48cc138b2810",
                                                "text": "With so much construction and renovation going on all around him, he was more or less living in a new city now, as it were. [His city is not newly founded, and it has been neither renamed nor moved, but in some practical way it is true that he does not live in the same city that he used to live in.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bfe02346-0152-4ef6-b559-20cd2a611c7f",
                                                "sense_id": "c2077c22-c50d-33af-a309-48cc138b2810",
                                                "text": "God brought them out of Egypt; he hath as it were the ſtrength of an Vnicorne."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8ad4af9-b73c-48e6-8dca-928de820e6c2",
                                                "sense_id": "c2077c22-c50d-33af-a309-48cc138b2810",
                                                "text": "Yet so strong is the parental ambition among those Polygons who are, as it were, on the fringe of the Circular class, that it is very rare to find a Nobleman of that position in society, who has neglected to place his first-born in the Circular Neo-Therapeutic Gymnasium before he has attained the age of a month."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c166106-0b3e-4dbd-9e46-765fa546115d",
                                                "sense_id": "c2077c22-c50d-33af-a309-48cc138b2810",
                                                "text": "[T]here was no very clear vision, to these people, of supra-mundane beings, sitting apart and ordaining the affairs of earth, as it were from a distance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f515c1ee-b2b9-3f4d-afc8-bf9880e4f807",
                                        "entry_id": "4612d932-69cf-355d-b329-9224f97fbad0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to draw attention to the use of a metaphor, sometimes to prevent confusion or to highlight wordplay."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d73d1a1c-f418-464e-9c24-8eef4987c565",
                                                "sense_id": "f515c1ee-b2b9-3f4d-afc8-bf9880e4f807",
                                                "text": "She gave all of the women seated at the restaurant food for thought, as it were."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cd10c10-0830-46fd-a2c1-171a27d246cb",
                                                "sense_id": "f515c1ee-b2b9-3f4d-afc8-bf9880e4f807",
                                                "text": "Concerns that cloud seeding might “steal” water from an area a cloud is traveling toward—robbing Peter to water Paul, as it were—have been dispelled."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6be5575-a960-4ba7-97b7-4df2c36cf176",
                                                "sense_id": "f515c1ee-b2b9-3f4d-afc8-bf9880e4f807",
                                                "text": "Scientists hope Crispr might also be used for genomic surgery, as it were, to correct errant genes that cause disease."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36dab8db-3214-4e8c-951c-0c0f5088c4de",
                                                "sense_id": "f515c1ee-b2b9-3f4d-afc8-bf9880e4f807",
                                                "text": "The Volkswagen diesel-emissions exploit was caused by a software failing, even if it seems to have been engineered, as it were, deliberately-"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "778ac5fb-378e-4cd2-8993-29844dee7d36",
                                                "sense_id": "f515c1ee-b2b9-3f4d-afc8-bf9880e4f807",
                                                "text": "Congress ended the bracero program in 1964, and the next 15 years were the salad days, as it were, for farmworkers"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a9d5529f-6738-4abc-b5de-afdba0022bc2",
                        "source_entry_id": "a0a1a4ec-dbab-3740-a486-fe5bc80d124c",
                        "source_sense_id": "0e6e45d3-2819-3372-be6f-89ddc8e5a333",
                        "source_sense_description": "in einem gewissen Sinn",
                        "target_lang_word": "so to speak",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "so to speak",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09553b3c-2021-337b-a744-bf60d2284e39",
                                        "entry_id": "c097ba03-435c-3191-a994-8a4bdbf37142",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a manner of speaking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fb24813-a3c7-4f9c-8cb7-2139a33dcd72",
                                                "sense_id": "09553b3c-2021-337b-a744-bf60d2284e39",
                                                "text": "Then Tom girded up his loins, so to speak, and went to work to “get his verses.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4de6524c-e923-4d76-8e7e-0a0d6afafa94",
                                                "sense_id": "09553b3c-2021-337b-a744-bf60d2284e39",
                                                "text": "This could have occurred nowhere but in England, where men and sea interpenetrate, so to speak—the sea entering into the life of most men, and the men knowing something or everything about the sea, in the way of amusement, of travel, or of bread-winning."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06294950-ac78-4f46-b6c0-fb4b45a87056",
                                                "sense_id": "09553b3c-2021-337b-a744-bf60d2284e39",
                                                "text": "He took the great, round world in his hand, so to speak, familiarly, contemptuously, and it seemed no larger than the seed of a Maraschino cherry in a table d’hôte grape fruit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07ba73c9-7f75-49e3-bdce-2c3876aa2c56",
                                                "sense_id": "09553b3c-2021-337b-a744-bf60d2284e39",
                                                "text": "I don't believe Lecter's even seen a woman in eight years. And oh, are you ever his taste. So to speak."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b123dcad-bd3f-46c1-82c9-514a627acaeb",
                                                "sense_id": "09553b3c-2021-337b-a744-bf60d2284e39",
                                                "text": "For Firefighter Joseph Ceravolo, President Obama turned up the heat, so to speak, even before he sat down to an early lunch on Thursday."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f76bb4fb-0980-4db2-9f97-29e82fe6c58f",
                                                "sense_id": "09553b3c-2021-337b-a744-bf60d2284e39",
                                                "text": "Every guest is appalled and fantastically humourless about the experience, even at this distance. You cannot help but wonder at cultural divides and how differently the British might have approached – or at least recalled – such events, at least in the early days. For us, surely, it would be a story for the ages. You could dine out on it for ever, so to speak."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1370bf39-9a90-4f34-bbda-3485974cf871",
                        "source_entry_id": "a0a1a4ec-dbab-3740-a486-fe5bc80d124c",
                        "source_sense_id": "0e6e45d3-2819-3372-be6f-89ddc8e5a333",
                        "source_sense_description": "in einem gewissen Sinn",
                        "target_lang_word": "in a way",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "in a way",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1df98d4-88bb-3708-bba4-42269e73b562",
                                        "entry_id": "f84a7045-864c-39f4-b9d1-d3755f3e6dde",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To a certain degree; to an extent; in a certain sense."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e29bbbb1-1b10-4403-8b3e-240138cedf8b",
                                                "sense_id": "d1df98d4-88bb-3708-bba4-42269e73b562",
                                                "text": "As an adult, I became a journalist whose beat is the environment. In a way, I’ve turned my youthful preoccupations into a profession."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f824a599-b3c3-49be-bf7e-ce2df96ffbed",
                        "source_entry_id": "a0a1a4ec-dbab-3740-a486-fe5bc80d124c",
                        "source_sense_id": "0e6e45d3-2819-3372-be6f-89ddc8e5a333",
                        "source_sense_description": "in einem gewissen Sinn",
                        "target_lang_word": "to a certain extent",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5d49f1a4-d264-4652-a0f1-a55dd8cbc1e4",
                        "source_entry_id": "a0a1a4ec-dbab-3740-a486-fe5bc80d124c",
                        "source_sense_id": "0e6e45d3-2819-3372-be6f-89ddc8e5a333",
                        "source_sense_description": "in einem gewissen Sinn",
                        "target_lang_word": "en quelque sorte",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "en quelque sorte",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8de1f7ac-1042-30db-9a61-e58fdbb86857",
                                        "entry_id": "4ee584f8-ca0b-30ac-9bfa-2f23c584c633",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Presque ; pour ainsi dire ; pratiquement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "235addab-ddcf-4d0c-ae38-b1e47d58fad0",
                                                "sense_id": "8de1f7ac-1042-30db-9a61-e58fdbb86857",
                                                "text": "Le territoire de Mostaganem et de Mazagran comprend trois villes distinctes : Mostaganem, Matamore et Mazagran. De ces trois villes, Mostaganem est la plus importante ; Matamore en est en quelque sorte la citadelle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17e8daf1-89bf-4a1a-8a6e-790b4c04091d",
                                                "sense_id": "8de1f7ac-1042-30db-9a61-e58fdbb86857",
                                                "text": "[…], puis M. Goulden tira de l’armoire une bouteille de son vin de Metz, qu’il gardait pour les grandes circonstances, et nous soupâmes en quelque sorte comme deux camarades ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8064fbb8-03c4-4315-839c-f1e5529cccef",
                                                "sense_id": "8de1f7ac-1042-30db-9a61-e58fdbb86857",
                                                "text": "La courbe d’aimantation stable passe par l’origine ; c’est en quelque sorte, la courbe médiane entre les deux branches de la courbe d’hystérésis."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a299470-a108-49d3-9750-22a64709579e",
                                                "sense_id": "8de1f7ac-1042-30db-9a61-e58fdbb86857",
                                                "text": "Les oscillations du foliot constituent en quelque sorte une horloge dans l'horloge. Elles rythment le mouvement des aiguilles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6be019c-ba21-4974-8a90-a6e18af0e8cd",
                                                "sense_id": "8de1f7ac-1042-30db-9a61-e58fdbb86857",
                                                "text": "Chaque soirée passée à ses côtés m'aidait à avancer à pas de géant dans mon domaine. Il était devenu mon coach privé en quelque sorte."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95ee538f-855a-44a8-806c-c3269b222495",
                                                "sense_id": "8de1f7ac-1042-30db-9a61-e58fdbb86857",
                                                "text": "— Grand-mère… elle s’est suicidée, en quelque sorte ?\nEncore aujourd’hui quand j’y pense cette question me bouleverse, non pas son sens mais sa forme, ce en quelque sorte dans la bouche d’un enfant de neuf ans, une précaution à mon endroit, une manière de tâter le terrain, d’y aller sur la pointe des pieds."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cea18611-658b-4b46-aaea-cfecf5106713",
                        "source_entry_id": "a0a1a4ec-dbab-3740-a486-fe5bc80d124c",
                        "source_sense_id": "0e6e45d3-2819-3372-be6f-89ddc8e5a333",
                        "source_sense_description": "in einem gewissen Sinn",
                        "target_lang_word": "pour ainsi dire",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pour ainsi dire",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ca10b872-303e-3650-b5b6-3c76097c98a5",
                                        "entry_id": "ed585c96-43bb-3df0-8ea8-8409b5db94c4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Quasiment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "note": "S’emploie lorsqu’on veut affaiblir ce qu’il peut y avoir d’exagéré dans l’expression dont on se sert, ou faire excuser ce qu’elle a d’extraordinaire, d’inusité",
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6f73a95-08b4-4791-9b27-eb9ce35be8df",
                                                "sense_id": "ca10b872-303e-3650-b5b6-3c76097c98a5",
                                                "text": "Au retour je voulus voir Herculanum, cette ville que l'on venoit pour ainsi dire d’exhumer ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29d36a90-02c9-4390-b6ef-1953ac06abc6",
                                                "sense_id": "ca10b872-303e-3650-b5b6-3c76097c98a5",
                                                "text": "Ce soc est fort petit, et le coutre qui ne fait qu'écorcher la terre , pour ainsi dire ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b46a9209-30ed-49cc-b9c8-f28fdd333168",
                                                "sense_id": "ca10b872-303e-3650-b5b6-3c76097c98a5",
                                                "text": "L’eau nécessaire à la respiration pénètre par l’une des ouvertures, est chassée par l’autre, grâce aux contractions du manteau, et, sortant avec rapidité, refoule pour ainsi dire en sens contraire l’animal, qui nage seulement à l’aide des mouvemens respiratoires."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14c39295-019d-43dc-a61f-bae252463fc2",
                                                "sense_id": "ca10b872-303e-3650-b5b6-3c76097c98a5",
                                                "text": "Parmi les forces connues de ce géant des mondes des 4ᵉ et 5ᵉ dimensions se trouvait une substance —BAL— laquelle , mise en mouvement dans une certaine direction sous l’influence d'instruments propulsifs […], « électrocutait » pour ainsi dire toutes les formes de vie animée qu'elle pénétrait."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa129e86-0028-4909-9bdb-051d18b0f05c",
                                                "sense_id": "ca10b872-303e-3650-b5b6-3c76097c98a5",
                                                "text": "Et ce ne fut pas une lente décadence qui surprit le monde européanisé ; les civilisations antiques pourrirent et s’effritèrent ; la civilisation européanisée sauta d’un coup, pour ainsi dire. En l’espace de cinq ans, elle fut entièrement ébranlée et détruite."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f04b213b-6802-45ad-8cfa-7927a44f23fe",
                                                "sense_id": "ca10b872-303e-3650-b5b6-3c76097c98a5",
                                                "text": "Quelques graveurs, surtout M. Marcellin-Legrand, ont cherché et ont réussi en partie à modifier l’œil des sept chiffres grands devenus pour ainsi dire les plus petits (depuis le 3 jusqu'au 9), afin de pallier leur disparate intolérable ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcdbd3b6-b052-4f73-8b20-30053f1674a0",
                                                "sense_id": "ca10b872-303e-3650-b5b6-3c76097c98a5",
                                                "text": "Je la tapais, mais tendrement pour ainsi dire…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "747801d5-38d3-40d4-8494-dfa8cdeecb8c",
                                                "sense_id": "ca10b872-303e-3650-b5b6-3c76097c98a5",
                                                "text": "Rien de plus dégradé, de plus nu, de plus misérable à l’oeil que cette quadruple façade percée d’une multitude de fenêtres grillées auxquelles se tenaient collés, du bas en haut, une foule de visages maigres et blêmes, pressés les uns au-dessus des autres, comme les pierres d’un mur, et tous pour ainsi dire encadrés dans les entre-croisements des barreaux de fer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
